1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,780
When I woke up this morning,

2
00:00:07,780 --> 00:00:12,000
I found myself smack in the middle

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,100
of another weird-ass situation.

4
00:00:23,280 --> 00:00:27,280
Oh, for crying out loud, another one?

5
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:29,980
These freaky creature things are coming out of the woods.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Good work!

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,000
I can hear my heart, and how do you think you know?

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:40,000
The heart of the moon will be.

9
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,000
The beginning was that time.

10
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
You were suddenly suddenly in the eye.

11
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:02,000
The moment you appeared before you came out.

12
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,000
You were the one who was chosen.

13
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,000
You were the one who was chosen.

14
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:07,000
You were the one who was chosen.

15
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:08,000
You were the one who was chosen.

16
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,000
You were the one who was chosen.

17
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:10,000
You were the one who was chosen.

18
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,000
You were the one who was chosen.

19
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:15,000
You were the one who was chosen!

20
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,000
You were a man who was chosen.

21
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:45,980
Thank you.

22
00:01:46,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Good morning, everybody.

23
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,140
Looks like it's going to be another hot one in Fukuoka today.

24
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:20,160
We're going to have to break out the parasols, fans, water bottles, hate, whatever you've got.

25
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:21,880
Hey, Icarus.

26
00:02:22,160 --> 00:02:22,800
Yes, Master?

27
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:24,380
Who the hell is that?

28
00:02:24,460 --> 00:02:25,320
Is she from your world?

29
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,640
She's got wings like you.

30
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:27,560
I'm not sure.

31
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:29,700
Well, she certainly looks like you.

32
00:02:29,780 --> 00:02:32,900
I mean, not just the wings, the collar, the weird ear thingies.

33
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:36,660
You do not get to make my home into your new clubhouse for freaky angel girls.

34
00:02:36,740 --> 00:02:37,640
Is this sinking in?

35
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:39,620
Hey, Mr. Littlebug.

36
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:48,840
I hope I didn't hear what I thought I just heard.

37
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:50,700
I'm sorry.

38
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:52,200
What was that you called me there?

39
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:53,960
I called you Mr. Littlebug.

40
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:56,380
Who else in the room would I be calling Mr.?

41
00:02:56,380 --> 00:02:56,880
Right.

42
00:02:57,100 --> 00:02:57,640
Thanks.

43
00:02:57,640 --> 00:03:02,080
Icarus, you know my motto?

44
00:03:02,300 --> 00:03:04,160
Peace and quiet is the only way to live?

45
00:03:04,780 --> 00:03:07,760
I'm having a hell of a time maintaining that with just you here.

46
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:08,960
See what I'm getting at?

47
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:10,040
Yes, Master.

48
00:03:10,780 --> 00:03:13,300
Hey, move your ass and get this chick out of here!

49
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,380
Enough's enough already!

50
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:17,440
Let me get back to my peace and quiet!

51
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:20,420
Everyone always seems to have such a good time at Tomoki.

52
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:22,740
Who's in there?

53
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:28,500
Why do we have to bring her along again?

54
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:29,460
Who cares?

55
00:03:29,640 --> 00:03:30,520
The more the merrier.

56
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,280
At least that's always been my philosophy.

57
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:35,280
I don't think that's true in this case.

58
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:39,360
Originally, Tomo and I were supposed to go to the beach by ourselves today.

59
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,000
See how well that worked out.

60
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:46,700
Yes!

61
00:03:46,820 --> 00:03:47,360
A winner!

62
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:50,380
Top prize is a day trip for two to the beach!

63
00:03:50,420 --> 00:03:52,020
You kids have a great time!

64
00:03:52,020 --> 00:03:52,380
Yeah!

65
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:54,480
Here you go.

66
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:55,340
Congratulations.

67
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:56,800
I did it!

68
00:03:56,860 --> 00:03:57,460
I won!

69
00:03:57,640 --> 00:04:00,840
You realize the two of us haven't been on a trip together since we were kids?

70
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:01,920
You played enough.

71
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,120
You were bound to win something.

72
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:04,660
Oh, I cannot wait!

73
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:07,720
And I'm so happy the rest of the gang won't be joining.

74
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:09,100
Congratulations!

75
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:11,020
I'm so excited for you.

76
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:13,360
You both won a day trip for two to the beach.

77
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:14,480
I can't believe it!

78
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:15,520
What a great day!

79
00:04:15,780 --> 00:04:16,100
Really!

80
00:04:16,100 --> 00:04:16,160
Really!

81
00:04:20,420 --> 00:04:22,800
Sorry, Sahara.

82
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:23,960
Why?

83
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,280
What are you sorry for?

84
00:04:25,580 --> 00:04:29,360
Because I know that you were supposed to be going on this trip just you and Tomoko.

85
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:29,700
No!

86
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:30,600
Forget it!

87
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:32,620
I'm cool with the way things turned out.

88
00:04:33,520 --> 00:04:35,380
Guess I can't stay disappointed forever.

89
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:37,400
I mean, hey, it's still a day at the beach.

90
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:39,760
So do you have a name or do we have to give you one?

91
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:41,440
It's Nymph.

92
00:04:42,320 --> 00:04:44,440
Okay, weird, but Nymph it is, I suppose.

93
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:46,580
Oh, yeah, I almost forgot.

94
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:49,440
I made breakfast rice balls for all of us.

95
00:04:49,940 --> 00:04:50,720
Here you go.

96
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:53,360
Take your pick.

97
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:56,360
Oh, this one.

98
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:59,440
Why has another Angeloid appeared here seemingly out of the blue?

99
00:04:59,500 --> 00:05:00,520
That's what I said.

100
00:05:00,600 --> 00:05:02,160
They're coming out of the freaking woodwork.

101
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:02,380
Wow!

102
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:05,020
Your wings glow rainbow colors all over.

103
00:05:05,140 --> 00:05:06,180
They're just beautiful.

104
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:08,840
You seem a lot different from Icarus, that's for sure.

105
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:10,440
Of course I seem different.

106
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:11,640
I'm not an alpha type.

107
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:12,920
So what are you?

108
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:17,420
I guess you'd call me the generation after alpha, if generation's the right word.

109
00:05:17,600 --> 00:05:20,380
With you side by side like that, you could pass for sisters.

110
00:05:20,880 --> 00:05:22,900
One of them, two of them, it's all the same.

111
00:05:23,360 --> 00:05:24,420
Just keep an eye on them.

112
00:05:24,420 --> 00:05:26,040
It's not the same at all.

113
00:05:26,180 --> 00:05:28,600
I just want my peace and quiet back.

114
00:05:31,020 --> 00:05:31,460
Whoa.

115
00:05:32,980 --> 00:05:33,460
Boobies!

116
00:05:34,180 --> 00:05:35,380
Boobie time!

117
00:05:41,460 --> 00:05:43,300
Better be careful, Tomoki.

118
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:50,100
Come on.

119
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,800
Where did you all get those swimsuits?

120
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:55,360
Prez felt bad for the girls, so she bought them.

121
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:57,460
Icarus, what happened to your back?

122
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:58,380
I don't see your wings.

123
00:05:58,760 --> 00:05:59,320
Correct.

124
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:02,320
I am able to withdraw my wings whenever I need to.

125
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:04,340
But they are still here.

126
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,060
This is as small as they get.

127
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:09,020
I can actually make my wings invisible.

128
00:06:09,980 --> 00:06:10,320
Oh.

129
00:06:10,860 --> 00:06:11,980
That sounds pretty useful.

130
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:15,100
I asked them to prop us up an umbrella over there.

131
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:17,160
What say we all go enjoy ourselves?

132
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:18,440
This is going to be awesome!

133
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,380
Nymph kind of bugs the crap out of me.

134
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,320
Hey, Eve.

135
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,500
We're never going to make it unless you pick up the pace.

136
00:06:24,660 --> 00:06:27,120
Mizuki, you're never going to find happiness, Eve.

137
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:29,660
Oh, screw her.

138
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:32,880
I'm at the beach, and I am going to have me some fun.

139
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:34,680
Service.

140
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:36,520
Set!

141
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:38,840
It's just like I dreamed it.

142
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:41,040
Beach volleyball is a beautiful sport.

143
00:06:41,380 --> 00:06:43,520
The way Sohara's chest heaves and bounces.

144
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:44,860
Best day ever!

145
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:47,500
